---
title: Avoid whole sources and companies, not just skills
date: 2026-09-16
summary: A new Avoid tab on your profile lets you exclude job sources and companies, alongside skills — one place for everything you don't want to see.
type: changelog
tags:
  - profile
  - job-seekers
  - filters
draft: false
---

Skills to avoid have lived on the Skills tab for a while — a way to tell your
profile "don't count this against me" without cluttering the skills you actually
have. It made sense there when it was the only thing to avoid, but it wasn't
built to grow.

Now it has: open [your profile](/my/profile) and there's a new **Avoid** tab.
Skills to avoid moved there, and it's joined by two new lists — sources to avoid
and companies to avoid. Had a bad experience with a recruiter who always posts
through the same ATS? Exclude that source. Burned by one employer specifically?
Exclude the company. Each list is independent, optional, and saved the moment you
add or remove something.
